<node id="Latinos">
  <data key="d0">Latinos</data>
  <data key="d1">group</data>
  <data key="d2">Latinos are a demographic group in the United States who have seen improvements in their personal financial situation since the Great Recession and are increasingly confident in their personal finances. They are also increasingly optimistic about their personal finances and expect upward mobility for their children. Latinos have specific economic conditions and outlooks, and their views on their children's financial futures vary. This demographic group is part of a broader category of Hispanics, as surveyed by the PEW RESEARCH CENTER.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1907f29be90571f9ffcda4b2841c8e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ab036de78d61714bf47e501a811c19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1cb33819e4bd6c1d057fa6c3509018f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4685a8d7626394b5ed73ecc6b964ecae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6380c2e8f0c4e8f8887468340bc0071d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db196f5cf13b5838df29dfc7a60b3fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f7a37181bc78b429ba629dce8fa4a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f090473fd475b5ea69ebf13b4ebb884</data>
